ook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>GOHDA SHUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDE MASAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIHARA KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>GOHDA, SHUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDE, MASAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIHARA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A PVAt cleaning sponge roller capable of enhancing durability without compromising a cleaning performance, the cleaning sponge roller (1) being constituted of a polyvinylacetal porous material having an elasticity in a wet condition, having a generally cylindrical roll body (3) and a plurality of protrusions (5) formed integrally on the outer peripheral surface (3a) of the roll body (3), and being adapted to clean an object with the tops (5a) of the protrusions (5) in a rotating contact with the object.  The protrusions (5) each have a tapering projection base (11) extending from the outer peripheral surface (3a) of the roll body (3) and a projection end (13) having a generally equal sectional shape from the tip face (11b) of the projection base (11) to the top (5a).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un rouleau éponge de nettoyage en PVAL servant à améliorer la durabilité sans affecter les propriétés nettoyantes. Ce rouleau éponge de nettoyage (1) se compose d'un matériau poreux de polyvinylacétal élastique dans des conditions d'humidité, ayant un corps généralement cylindrique (3) et une pluralité de protubérances (5) solidaires de la surface périphérique externe (3a) du corps (3) du rouleau. Ce rouleau est adapté pour nettoyer un objet avec les parties supérieures (5a) des protubérances (5) en contact par rotation avec l'objet. Ces protubérances (5) présentent chacune une base saillante effilée (11) s'étendant de la surface périphérique externe (3a) du corps (3) du rouleau et une extrémité saillante (13) se présentant sous forme de section généralement égale depuis la face d'extrémité (11b) de la base saillante (11) vers le haut (5a).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>